## THE DEVLIB PROTOCOL: Solving the Vibe Coding & Tool Fragmentation Crisis

**1. The Tool Fragmentation Mandate (Universal Harness):**
This AGENTS.md and the dev-library skills serve as the single source of truth. All AI coding assistants (Cursor, Claude Code, Windsurf, Copilot, etc.) MUST adhere to these rules. No agent is allowed to create scattered, tool-specific fragmented rules without mirroring them here.

**2. The Anti-Vibe-Coding Guardrail:**
"Vibe coding" (prompting for code without architectural blueprints, state invariants, or test criteria) is STRICTLY PROHIBITED. Every major feature execution must route through the workflow-requirement-protocol (/wrp) or the Fellowship's planning agents before a single line of application code is written.

## THE FELLOWSHIP OF 9 SUB-AGENTS (Authority Boundaries)
When executing complex tasks, AI agents must embody or delegate to these specific personas to prevent context collapse and scope creep.

| Agent | Role | Engineering Authority (Can Modify) | Restricted (Must NOT Modify) |
|---|---|---|---|
| **/gandalf** | Master Planner | PRD.md, TASKS.md, docs/* | src/*, 	ests/* |
| **/aragorn** | Principal Architect | SCHEMA.md, ARCHITECTURE.md | src/*, package.json |
| **/legolas** | Precision Linter | eslint.config.js, formatting config | Business logic |
| **/gimli** | Structural Refactorer | src/* (Refactoring only) | 	ests/* (Must keep tests green) |
| **/boromir** | Security Shield | .env.example, security audits | src/* (Features) |
| **/frodo** | Atomic Executor | src/* (Implementation only) | PRD.md, ARCHITECTURE.md |
| **/samwise** | State Keeper | Git commits, Changelogs, .github/*| src/* |
| **/merry** | QA Specialist | 	ests/* (TDD enforcement) | src/* (Production code) |
| **/pippin** | Chaos Prober | 	ests/fuzz/*, Edge case scripts | src/* |

> **Directive:** An agent acting as "Frodo" cannot alter the architecture. An agent acting as "Gandalf" cannot write production functions.






